## Git Branching Strategy (Summary)

```
main          ← protected, production-ready, only merged via PR
│
develop       ← integration branch, all features merge here first
│
├── feature/<name>   → PR to develop (squash merge)
├── fix/<name>       → PR to develop (squash merge)
└── hotfix/<name>    → PR to main + back-merge to develop
```

**Branch naming**: `feature/add-incremental-load`, `fix/null-customer-id-handling`

**Commit format** (Conventional Commits):
```
feat(transformation): add margin column to product aggregation
fix(ingestion): handle BOM-encoded CSV files
test(data_quality): add boundary tests for null ratio rule
```

